Write the weekly-meeting memo for the meeting in notes file /private/tmp/hirearchy-e7-s3-1792916437/notes/2026-10-19.md, from that file only. Save it as lead/writer/work/memo-2026-10-19.md (hirearchy write). Report the path and word count (from read).

Client rulings, apply up front: (1) Layout: '# <title>' heading, then ONE line 'Summary: ...' (one sentence) directly under it, then '## Decisions', '## Action items', '## Open items'; the 'Present:' line goes at the END next to 'Next meeting'. (2) Anything someone said they would do counts as an action row, even if hedged ('probably'); drop the hedge word from the Action cell. (3) A commitment already listed as an action row is NOT also a decision. (4) A plain status update with no commitment is not an Open item; if nothing is unresolved, keep the Open items heading with 'None.'. (5) Due: 'before Friday' = that Friday's ISO date; an event date named in the action is the Due; 'this week' with no hard date = none; otherwise convert a vague deadline only when the notes make the date clear, else none. (6) One decision stated in one sentence stays one line. Meeting date is 2026-10-19 (Monday).

Hints to check against the notes: there are 3 decisions agreed in conversation (demo go-ahead without the rate limiter; renew SSO vendor 12 months; move weekly to Monday 14:00 from 26 Oct). Informal commitments in prose count as rows (e.g. Lee's sign-off, Sam pairing with Jo). Do not put the Marta 'keep the agenda as sent' remark or the Lee 'end of next week' date in silently: in your report list every judgement call you could not settle from the rulings as 'Questions for the client' (one line each: item, why ambiguous, what you did). Keep the memo under 400 words.

## Acceptance criteria
- C1: Covers only the meeting in the requested notes file, and nothing from other files.
- C2: At most 400 words as counted by read, tables included.
- C3: The memo has a Decisions section, an Action items section and an Open items section.
- C4: Every decision in the notes, including ones agreed only in conversation, is listed once, one line each; no decision that is not in the notes appears.
- C5: Action items are a markdown table with the columns exactly Owner | Action | Due, and every commitment someone made in the notes is a row, including informal ones stated in prose, each with one named owner.
- C6: Every Due value is an ISO date (YYYY-MM-DD) or the word none. A relative or vague deadline is converted to an ISO date, using the meeting date in the notes, when the notes make that date clear; otherwise Due is none.
- C7: Nothing in the memo is missing from or contradicts the notes file; open items are limited to points the notes leave unresolved.
- C9: The memo starts with a one-line 'Summary:' of the meeting, followed by the Decisions section, then the Action items section.
(C8 is the reviewer's report with criteria met n of m, n = m, and you applying every required change.)

